1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:19,368
Most trading bots just run hardcoded rules. Ours is different. This is a true autonomous
agent: a large language model, Claude, that thinks, analyzes the market, and makes its own
trading decisions through tool calling. And it speaks directly to the official Alpaca M C
P server. Let me show you.

2
00:00:20,368 --> 00:00:39,496
When it runs, the agent boots the official Alpaca M C P server, and seventy-four tools
become available instantly — stocks, crypto, options, portfolio. Notice the agent doesn't
just buy. It first calls tools to inspect the account, pull price snapshots, and read the
news. Then it decides.

3
00:00:40,496 --> 00:01:03,752
Here it decides. For N-VIDIA it buys, but deliberately sizes to just eight percent of
equity — below its fifteen percent cap — because earnings are this week. For Bitcoin, even
though sentiment is bullish, it refuses to enter: R-S-I is eighty-two, parabolic. In its
own words: discipline wins, don't chase the top. This isn't an if-else statement. This is
judgment.

4
00:01:04,752 --> 00:01:22,968
Every decision blends two sides: technical analysis — R-S-I, moving averages, momentum —
and news sentiment that Claude scores itself. And there's a hard guardrail: a per-order
cap. When an order exceeds it, the agent adapts on its own instead of crashing. A-I, plus
a safety rail.

5
00:01:23,968 --> 00:01:53,800
We don't just claim results. A one-year backtest gives real metrics: return, Sharpe ratio,
max drawdown, win-rate, versus buy and hold. On calm markets like the S-P-Y, our trend
strategy delivers a Sharpe of one point four with a small drawdown. On highly volatile
stocks, the mechanical strategy loses to buy and hold — and that is exactly why we put
L-L-M reasoning and sentiment on top of raw signals. We know precisely when this approach
is strong, and when it isn't.

6
00:01:54,800 --> 00:02:11,456
One brain, two tool backends: a lightweight local layer, or the official Alpaca M C P
server. Everything is paper-trading, safe, with full reasoning logged. Autonomous,
transparent, and built right on top of the Alpaca ecosystem. Thank you.
